Xiaomi Pad 5 (nabu) adaptation for Skyward Recovery
Device maintainer: Seimo
https://github.com/SeimoDev
https://x.com/SeimoDev

Skyward Recovery is developed by kirklin and contributors:
https://github.com/kirklin/skyward
The adaptation and Skyward patches are distributed under GPL-3.0,
as provided in LICENSE. Upstream copyright and license notices remain
in the corresponding source files.

The build extracts the existing recovery ramdisk, kernel, firmware and
Android/Qualcomm libraries from:
HyperOS_4.0.0.41_nabu_A17_by_zxcwsurx_20260920.zip
These components retain their respective original licenses.
The extraction inventory is recorded in proprietary-files.txt and
materials.json. The ROM must be supplied to rebuild an image.

The kernel is reused from the ROM boot image:
4.14.180-moon-os3-ga5805c039, built 2026-04-03.
The matching Moon kernel binary distribution is mirrored at:
https://github.com/sticpaper/moon_kernel_mirror/tree/main/nabu/20260403
kernel/nabu.config records the embedded build configuration.
The mirror contains distributed kernel binaries; it is not presented
as the kernel's corresponding source tree.

The original recovery's Android runtime and TWRP components, AOSP VNDK 30,
and the supplied ROM's hardware services provide the base environment.
MiSans and Kirk Mono are supplied by the pinned Skyward source; their
licenses are preserved by Skyward's packer.
